#!/usr/bin/env perl

use 5.040;
use re '/aasx';
use warnings FATAL => 'all';

use FindBin::libs;

use Mojolicious::Commands();

=head1 SYNOPSIS

Run a command of the job queue of tCMS.

=head2 USAGE

    bin/tcms-jobs minion worker -j 1
    bin/tcms-jobs minion job -s

Run it from the root of the tCMS install, because the paths of the queue are
relative to it.  C<minion worker> takes the jobs out of the queue and runs
them, so keep one running as a service.  The C<-j> option is how many jobs run
at once.  A transcode uses all the cores, so 1 is right.  The other commands of
Minion, such as C<minion job>, show and manage the jobs.

See L<Trog::Jobs::App>.

=cut

Mojolicious::Commands->start_app( 'Trog::Jobs::App', @ARGV );
